      },
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In my environment, there was an avatar that became an error robot, even though it was a recently used avatar.\n\nSpecifically, this is the avatar we used in the event on 2024-10-29, a week ago.\n\nMoreover, even if it was an avatar that was recently uploaded, there was also an error robot. Thus, it seems that both the upload time and recent usage have no relation in my environment.\n\n> So, I suspect that something like a security system cache has been corrupted, causing the request to return an error once. After a while, the system caches the data and responds normally.\n\nI support this theory, and a concern has been raised.\n\nIn the future, if the cache of the corresponding data is lost due to a server failure, error robots like this will occur again in large numbers.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
